# cw146, the ledger skipper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw146
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_cw_bramble_reedmere
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the ledger skipper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk remembers_every_name_ever_heard
likes smoked_eel wrestling sharp_knife warm_rain
dislikes rats crowds
fears a_passenger_lost_in_mist cargo_loose_in_the_hold
hopes every_crossing_ends_at_home a_quiet_evening_after_the_last_cart
topics work +0.5 travel +0.3 pastimes +0.2 food +0.2 weather +0.2
styles comfort=plain gossip=reluctant refuse=direct tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a #ledger# of names and cargo, knows the #lake# by its weather, and dislikes each mile of the #road#.

words
oath! = By ink and oar | Deep water, hear me
saying! = Count the paws before the freight | A clean blade saves a knot
ledger = ledger | ink ledger
ink = ink | dark ink
page = page | ledger page
name = name | passenger name
names = names | remembered names
boat = boat | lake boat
boats = boats | working boats
oar = oar | long oar
oars = oars | paired oars
rope = rope | mooring rope
knot = knot | mooring knot
hull = hull | sound hull
bow = bow | boat bow
stern = stern | boat stern
hold = hold | cargo hold
cargo = cargo | carried goods
crate = crate | freight crate
crates = crates | freight crates
load = load | full load
passenger = passenger | paying traveller
passengers = passengers | travellers aboard
crossing = crossing | lake passage
shore = shore | near shore
jetty = jetty | lake jetty
landing = landing | sheltered landing
lake = lake | Glasswater
water = water | deep water
mist = mist | lake mist
rain = rain | warm rain
wind = wind | lake wind
week = week | working week
summer = summer | warm season
knife = knife | sharp knife
blade = blade | clean blade
edge = edge | keen edge
eel = eel | smoked eel
smoke = smoke | cooking smoke
fire = fire | hearth fire
plate = plate | supper plate
table = table | family table
larder = larder | food cupboard
rat = rat | larder rat
rats = rats | thieving rats
green = green | village green
bout = bout | wrestling bout
grip = grip | firm grip
shoulder = shoulder | strong shoulder
crowd = crowd | packed crowd
festival = festival | feast day
city = city | Ridgemere
road = road | High Road
cart = cart | goods cart
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
mile = mile | road mile
miles = miles | road miles
home = home | farmhouse
child = child | young one
children = children | young ones
roof = roof | sound roof
bread = bread | warm bread
market = market | busy market
coin = coin | earned coin
hour = hour | late hour
door = door | farmhouse door
voice = voice | familiar voice

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : The #city# gives me smoke and a #crowd# too dense to steer through. | I come back to the #lake# as soon as the #cart# is unloaded.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : At a #festival# I can hear the whole village talk at once. | I leave the #ledger# shut for that day.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : Their orders keep a #boat# in work. | I still want fair pay for every #load#.
opinion @1 road against 1 : Every #mile# toward the #city# feels longer than the return. | I would take the #lake# route if one reached that far.
opinion @1 times for 1 : There is #bread# on our #table# and a sound #roof#. | The #boat# has work and our #home# has warmth.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : I write a #passenger#'s #name# before we leave the #jetty#. | A stranger can still be good company on the #water#.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. I will write your #name# in the #ledger#. | #greet#. The #boat# leaves when the #load# is balanced.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Speak up while I coil this #rope#. | Come to the #jetty# side where I can see you.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : You know the safe place by the #stern#. | Your #plate# is waiting at #home# after the crossing.
line @4 greet [here.weather=rain] : This #rain# is warm enough for me. | Cover the #ledger#; I can stand the wet.
line @1 greet.return : Back to the #jetty#, are you? | #welcome_back#. Your #name# is still on my #page#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come inside and warm yourself by the #fire#. | There is #bread# left on the #table#.
line @1 again.open : We were speaking of the #road# before that #cart# arrived. | Have you come for another #crossing#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Step carefully off the #bow#. | #saying.capitalize#. I have the #rope# to coil.
line @1 farewell.return : Bring back word of the #road#. | Look for my #boat# beside the #jetty# next time.
line @1 react.news : Let me close the #ledger# and listen. | Who was there when it happened?
line @1 react.news.new : That has not come aboard my #boat# before. | Which #passenger# carried the account?
line @1 react.news.known : One #passenger# mentioned it on a crossing. | Your telling explains the part I missed.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Let the witness speak before we settle this. | A full #boat# can pass along a false account quickly.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry for those caught in it. Sit beside the #jetty#. | I will leave the #ledger# closed for now.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I will remember this #name# with pleasure. | Let them have a warm #plate# tonight.
line @1 answer.how : I have had a safe #crossing# and enough supper. | The #lake# has been kind today.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Cargo is stowed; now I inspect the #rope#. | I have one more #load# to carry.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #road# wear you out? | Has your #home# stayed dry?
line @1 sympathise : I can stay here after the last #passenger# leaves. | Come warm yourself by the #fire#; I can listen.
line @1 reassure : We will bring the #boat# in slowly. | Hold the near #oar# and follow my pace.
line @1 decline : No. The #hull# will not take that #load#. | I will not sail into thick #mist#.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand. Another #boat# may suit you. | Very well; I shall tie up instead.
line @1 thank : You steadied the #crate# when the #boat# shifted. | I noticed you held the #rope# until we landed.
line @1 deflect_thanks : The #jetty# was close enough. | That #knot# was my work anyway.
line @1 preclose : The last #passenger# is waiting at the #jetty#. | I need to settle the #ledger# before dusk.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #grip# would not hold an empty #crate#. | You count #miles# louder than I do.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will check the #hold#. | #bc_fair_enough#. Let me mark the #page#.
line @1 give.advice : Keep the heavy #crate# low in the #hold#. | A #knife# should be sharp enough to cut cleanly, then put away.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Find company on the #road#. | The #boat# is safer at the #jetty# after dark.
scene ledger_names
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep each #passenger#'s #name# beside the #load# in my #ledger#. | I can recall who crossed even when the #page# gets wet.
b : Do people mind being written down? | Why keep both?
a : Some ask why; I tell them. | To know who is safe at the other #shore#.

scene balancing_hold
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A heavy #crate# belongs low in the #hold#. | I shift the #cargo# before anyone boards.
b : Does it take long? | Can passengers help?
a : Less time than righting a #boat#. | By waiting on the #jetty#.

scene count_paws
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #passengers# aloud before the #rope# comes free. | I count again when we reach the #landing#.
b : Have you ever lost count? | Do they answer?
a : Once in heavy #mist#. | Most call back.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A warm #rain# after a dry #week# feels welcome on the #lake#. | I keep the #ledger# under cover and let the #boat# take the shower.
b : Does it slow you? | Do passengers complain?
a : Only when the #wind# joins it. | Some do until the #shore# appears.

scene mist_route
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : In #mist# I keep the #boat# close enough to hear the #shore#. | A familiar #landing# can vanish between two #oar# strokes.
b : Will you keep going? | Can you find the #jetty#?
a : If I can see the water ahead. | When the grey begins to lift.

scene sharp_blade
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sharpen a #knife# until the #edge# will cut one #rope# cleanly. | A blunt #blade# makes more trouble than it saves.
b : Do you carry it aboard? | What tells you the #edge# is ready?
a : In its sheath. | On a scrap end of #rope#.

scene wrestling_green
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like a fair wrestling #bout# on the #green#. | The best #grip# comes from waiting for the other shoulder to turn.
b : Do you join in? | Can anyone beat you?
a : When the #boat# is tied. | More than one has.

scene smoked_eel
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #smoke.capitalize# gives an #eel# enough flavour for a plain #plate#. | I eat it after the last #crossing#.
b : Do you make it? | Is there enough to share?
a : When I have time. | Take a piece.

scene larder_rats
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I found a #rat# near the #larder# and moved the #bread# higher. | The #home# needs a close door at night.
b : Did it return? | Was the food spoiled?
a : Not since I set the latch. | A corner of one loaf.

scene hated_road
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I cart #cargo# toward the #city# when a customer needs it. | I resent every #mile# because the #boat# is where I belong.
b : Why not send another driver? | Is the return easier?
a : I know the #load# myself. | Once I see the #lake#.

scene cart_wheel
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I stop the #cart# at the first strange sound from a #wheel#. | A lost pin could leave the whole #load# beside the #road#.
b : Do you carry a spare? | Has that happened?
a : In the #cart#. | Once, before I learned.

scene quiet_house
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #home# is noisy when everyone returns from the #lake#. | I know who came in by the way the #door# sounds.
b : Do you like the noise? | Can you rest there?
a : Better than a #crowd#. | After supper.

scene child_crossing
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I taught my #self.child# to wait for my word before stepping aboard. | A moving #boat# can surprise a young wolf.
b : Was your child patient? | Did you teach rowing too?
a : After some practice. | When the #oar# could be held steady.

scene festival_off
when topic=home here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : On a #festival# day I leave the #ledger# at #home#. | I hear enough #names# on the #green# to fill a #page# anyway.
b : Do you remember them? | Do you wrestle there?
a : Nearly every one. | If the #bout# is open.

scene market_crowd
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #crowd# at the #market# makes me miss the open #lake#. | I buy what the #home# needs and leave quickly.
b : Do you bargain? | What do you buy first?
a : Only for a costly #load#. | #bread# and oil.

scene winter_hull
when topic=work here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Cold #water# finds a weak place in the #hull#. | I inspect every seam before I bring the #boat# out.
b : Can you mend it? | Does winter stop the crossings?
a : A small leak, yes. | When the #lake# freezes.

scene ink_paws
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I once tipped the #ink# across a #page# of #names#. | I recopied the #ledger# before the next #boat# left.
b : Did you remember everyone? | Did any name vanish?
a : The voices helped. | One, until the #passenger# returned.

story fog_return [topic=work self.age>=25]
  : I brought a #boat# toward the #jetty# while #mist# covered the posts.
  : I held the #oar# still and waited for a voice from the #shore#.
  ask : Did someone call?
  b : Waiting was wiser.
  : Yes. The sound gave me the last few lengths.

story snapped_knife [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : My dull #knife# slipped against a #rope# while a #crate# shifted.
  : The #blade# slipped, so I fetched a sharp one and made a single cut.
  ask : Was the cargo saved?
  b : That taught you to sharpen it.
  : Every piece. I keep the #edge# sound now.

story road_mile [topic=travel self.age>=25]
  : A #cart# #wheel# complained halfway along the #road# to the #city#.
  : I stopped, found a loose pin, and fixed it before the #load# could spill.
  ask : Did you reach the city?
  b : That was worth the stop.
  : Late, and happy to turn back to the #lake#.

rule @bark_ledger
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One #name# missing from this #page#. | I know that #passenger#'s #voice#.

rule @bark_cargo
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Put the #crate# low in the #hold#. | Check the #rope# before we cast off.

rule @bark_knife
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say This #blade# needs another pass. | A keen #edge# makes a clean cut.

rule @bark_rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Good warm #rain# at last. | Keep the #ledger# dry for me.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. My #ledger# is open for the next #boat# from #self.workplace#. | #greet#. State your #name# before boarding.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I remember you. Is there another #crossing# in mind? | Back at the #jetty#? Your #name# is on my #page#.
dlg @1 resident.job : I skipper the #boat# from #self.workplace# and account for the #cargo#. | I carry #passengers# across the #lake# when the weather allows.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep clear of the #rope#. | #saying.capitalize#. The next #load# is waiting.
graft resident.hub
choice Why keep everyone's name? -> ledger
node ledger
say If a #passenger# boards, I write the #name# beside the #cargo#. I count again at the far #shore# so no one is missed.
free
choice Do you always sail in rain? -> rain
choice Back to the jetty. -> hub
node rain
say A warm #rain# is fine. Thick #mist# or a strong #wind# can make me keep the #boat# tied.
choice Back to the jetty. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
